.TH CW "1" "October 2026" "cw 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cw \- cw join
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cw
\fI\,join \/\fR[\fI\,OPTIONS\/\fR] \fI\,NAME\/\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IP
Add a window to an existing Context.
.IP
By default adds the current (focused) window. Use \fB\-\-ref\fR to add a specific
window by its reference number from `cw windows \fB\-\-all\fR`.
.IP
Examples:
.TP
cw join MyProject
add current window
.TP
cw join MyProject \fB\-\-ref\fR 3
add window #3 from `cw windows \fB\-\-all\fR`
.TP
cw join MyProject \fB\-r\fR 3 \fB\-w\fR Dev
add window #3 and name it "Dev"
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-window\-name\fR TEXT
Name for this window within the Context.
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-ref\fR INTEGER
Window ref number from `cw windows \fB\-\-all\fR`.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show this message and exit.
